Q: How can I configure an Angular application hosted in Firebase to correctly handle the Google auth handler URL? A: <p>You need to ensure that the Firebase Hosting configuration excludes the <code>__/</code> namespace from being rewritten to your Angular <code>index.html</code>.</p>
<p>In your <code>firebase.json</code>, your rewrites should look like this:</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>{
  &quot;hosting&quot;: {
    &quot;public&quot;: &quot;dist/your-project-name&quot;,
    &quot;ignore&quot;: [
      &quot;firebase.json&quot;,
      &quot;**/.*&quot;,
      &quot;**/node_modules/**&quot;
    ],
    &quot;rewrites&quot;: [
      {
        &quot;source&quot;: &quot;!/__/**&quot;,
        &quot;destination&quot;: &quot;/index.html&quot;
      }
    ]
  }
}
</code></pre>

Q: How to include html file in another html file and then alert result via JavaScript and jQuery A: <p>Instead of using jQuery, you could make use of JavaScript's <code>fetch()</code></p>
<p>Having a <code>b.html</code> file like requested:</p>
<p><sub>b.html</sub></p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;p&gt;Included HTML&lt;/p&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>inside any other page you could use:</p>
<p><sub>index.html</sub></p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div data-get=&quot;b.html&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;script type=&quot;module&quot;&gt;
  // Utils
  const els = (sel, par = document) =&gt; par.querySelectorAll(sel);
  const get = async (page) =&gt; (await fetch(page)).text();

  // Init
  console.log(await get(&quot;b.html&quot;)); // &quot;&lt;p&gt;Included HTML&lt;/p&gt;&quot;
  els(&quot;[data-get]&quot;).forEach(async el =&gt; el.innerHTML = await get(el.dataset.get));
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>And you can see above how you can either alert the response <em>.text()</em>, or even populate it into an existing element.</p>
<p>Find out more:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/78962263/383904">Dynamically load partial HTML into element</a></li>
<li><a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/79050681/383904">Load data from different HTML files with click event on list items</a></li>
</ul>
